WEBVTT

1
00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:06.535
Ninety-one, ninety-two...

2
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.208
- It's down there.
- Where? If they catch us...

3
00:02:09.409 --> 00:02:11.559
There's a million
bottles of booze in there.

4
00:02:11.578 --> 00:02:13.578
You think they're
gonna miss one?

5
00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:30.421
Weather is with us, sir.

6
00:02:30.797 --> 00:02:33.994
We arrive in port
in a couple of hours.

7
00:02:34.201 --> 00:02:35.964
Very good.

8
00:02:35.969 --> 00:02:37.969
You're welcome, sir.

9
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.008
Man, I never smelt
anything like this.

10
00:02:45.013 --> 00:02:46.942
Not even when you're
in the crapper.

11
00:02:46.947 --> 00:02:50.178
Oh, what, your shit
smells like roses?

12
00:02:50.383 --> 00:02:52.383
Hey, look.

13
00:02:52.819 --> 00:02:54.819
I'll give you a hand.

14
00:03:00.894 --> 00:03:02.736
- Thought you said
it was booze.

15
00:03:02.741 --> 00:03:04.741
That's what the papers said.

16
00:03:09.336 --> 00:03:11.636
Captain, we have a breach
in lower level. Look.

17
00:03:11.738 --> 00:03:13.738
- Which section?
- 101.

18
00:03:14.174 --> 00:03:15.670
Fuck. Take the wheel.

19
00:03:15.675 --> 00:03:17.675
- Yes, sir.
- Fuck.

20
00:03:19.146 --> 00:03:21.341
Close the door. Get the masks.

21
00:03:27.587 --> 00:03:29.714
Holy shit.

22
00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.390
Take care of them.

23
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.870
- Morning.
- Passport, please.

24
00:04:25.245 --> 00:04:26.841
Rough seas?

25
00:04:26.846 --> 00:04:28.648
The sea was smooth.
The party was a...

26
00:04:28.653 --> 00:04:30.312
bit rough, if you
know what I mean.

27
00:04:30.317 --> 00:04:32.047
- Ibiza.
- Yeah.

28
00:04:32.052 --> 00:04:34.052
Thanks.

29
00:04:44.097 --> 00:04:46.895
When I was a kid, my father
used to take me fishing.

30
00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.331
Never could figure out how
he knew where the fish were.

31
00:04:51.471 --> 00:04:54.907
They were always exactly
where he said they would be.

32
00:05:19.733 --> 00:05:21.463
Security check.

33
00:05:21.468 --> 00:05:23.365
Do I look like
a security risk?

34
00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.945
Please step out of the car and...

35
00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.950
bring your documents
to the office.

36
00:05:27.274 --> 00:05:29.037
My documents are
right here, sir.

37
00:05:29.042 --> 00:05:31.169
The computer is in the office.

38
00:05:32.712 --> 00:05:34.109
Her too.

39
00:05:34.114 --> 00:05:35.977
She's sleeping.

40
00:05:35.982 --> 00:05:38.746
- With her documents.
- Okay, sure.

41
00:05:53.667 --> 00:05:55.667
You're gonna lose it.

42
00:05:59.306 --> 00:06:01.306
Close, inspector,
you're close.

43
00:06:05.845 --> 00:06:07.845
That's a big one.
Go left, go left.

44
00:06:10.417 --> 00:06:12.417
Don't let him get away.

45
00:06:16.856 --> 00:06:18.856
You're close.

46
00:06:23.496 --> 00:06:25.496
Go left, go left. Go right.

47
00:06:28.735 --> 00:06:30.935
Must be Moby Dick you
hooked. Need some help?

48
00:06:31.104 --> 00:06:33.104
No, thank you, Frank.

49
00:06:33.506 --> 00:06:35.327
I have been fishing
these waters...

50
00:06:35.332 --> 00:06:37.332
since before you were born.

51
00:06:42.115 --> 00:06:45.516
You were close,
inspector. You were close.

52
00:06:49.089 --> 00:06:51.020
Good thing that we
French have such...

53
00:06:51.025 --> 00:06:53.025
a highly developed
sense of humor.

54
00:06:53.093 --> 00:06:54.922
With all due respect,
the French...

55
00:06:54.927 --> 00:06:56.691
think Jerry Lewis is a genius.

56
00:06:56.696 --> 00:06:59.824
- Jerry Lewis is a genius.
- Dean was the genius.

57
00:07:00.033 --> 00:07:03.093
No, Dean just stood there
with a drink and a cigarette.

58
00:07:03.303 --> 00:07:06.272
My point exactly. Anyone can
fall down and get a laugh.

59
00:07:06.473 --> 00:07:08.243
How many people can
do it standing...

60
00:07:08.248 --> 00:07:10.248
still with a drink
and a cigarette?

61
00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.451
I am afraid our day of
leisure is cut short.

62
00:07:24.657 --> 00:07:26.321
There is a mess in Marseilles.

63
00:07:26.326 --> 00:07:29.193
Some madman driving an
Audi at impossible speeds.

64
00:07:31.765 --> 00:07:33.765
Don't look at me.

65
00:07:33.867 --> 00:07:36.734
That is the first place
the chief told me to look.

66
00:07:36.936 --> 00:07:41.100
But I will tell him you
have the perfect alibi.

67
00:07:42.642 --> 00:07:44.642
As usual.

68
00:07:50.183 --> 00:07:52.183
Tarconi.

69
00:07:52.786 --> 00:07:54.416
- Please.
- I am sorry, Frank.

70
00:07:54.421 --> 00:07:57.515
- It's our first bite.
- Yeah, yeah.

71
00:07:58.258 --> 00:08:00.258
- Please.
- Yeah.

72
00:08:00.326 --> 00:08:01.990
Stop the boat. Come on.

73
00:08:01.995 --> 00:08:04.725
- No. No, Frank.
- Come on, please.

74
00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:48.531
Purpose of your
visit, Mr. Johnson?

75
00:08:49.308 --> 00:08:50.871
Business.

76
00:08:50.876 --> 00:08:52.706
What kind of business?

77
00:08:52.711 --> 00:08:54.711
Environmental protection.

78
00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:03.420
Thank you.

79
00:09:04.857 --> 00:09:06.484
Mr. Minister, you're
giving the...

80
00:09:06.489 --> 00:09:08.388
opening address at
an EU conference...

81
00:09:08.393 --> 00:09:11.243
...on environmental impact of
industry in Odessa tomorrow.

82
00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.256
- What is top on your
list of priorities?

83
00:09:13.261 --> 00:09:14.261
It's a short list.

84
00:09:14.266 --> 00:09:15.401
There's one item: the...

85
00:09:15.406 --> 00:09:17.197
environment and
how to protect it.

86
00:09:17.202 --> 00:09:19.202
In the face of
increasing pressure...

87
00:09:19.204 --> 00:09:20.673
...for industries to compete...

88
00:09:20.678 --> 00:09:22.336
successfully in a
global economy...

89
00:09:22.341 --> 00:09:24.110
...that goal can
sometimes come up...

90
00:09:24.115 --> 00:09:25.873
against some very
harsh realities.

91
00:09:25.878 --> 00:09:27.607
Well, not as harsh
as a polluted...

92
00:09:27.612 --> 00:09:29.042
and uninhabitable planet.

93
00:09:29.047 --> 00:09:30.944
Gentlemen, if you'll
excuse me now...

94
00:09:30.949 --> 00:09:34.146
...I have trees to save and
industrialists to disappoint.

95
00:09:37.856 --> 00:09:40.051
- Your speech for tomorrow.
- Any good?

96
00:09:40.592 --> 00:09:43.455
- It's going to piss
off a lot of people.

97
00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.460
Excellent.

98
00:10:07.586 --> 00:10:09.586
Hello?

99
00:10:09.788 --> 00:10:11.788
Mr. Minister?

100
00:10:12.591 --> 00:10:13.987
Who is this?

101
00:10:13.992 --> 00:10:16.290
My name is not important.

102
00:10:16.495 --> 00:10:18.745
I've been put in charge
of the negotiations...

103
00:10:18.931 --> 00:10:21.331
...you are engaged
in with Ecocorp...

104
00:10:21.533 --> 00:10:23.289
...for issuance of
their license...

105
00:10:23.294 --> 00:10:24.998
to do business in the Ukraine.

106
00:10:25.003 --> 00:10:27.503
You must be misinformed,
Mr. Whatever-Your-Name-Is.

107
00:10:27.673 --> 00:10:29.732
I've terminated
negotiations permanently.

108
00:10:29.942 --> 00:10:32.342
I think you will
reconsider that position...

109
00:10:32.544 --> 00:10:34.420
...once you have a
chance to study...

110
00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:36.425
the documents in the envelope.

111
00:10:50.862 --> 00:10:52.862
I'll be in touch.

112
00:11:34.139 --> 00:11:36.437
Yeah, there's
been an accident.

113
00:11:36.808 --> 00:11:40.141
Send an ambulance, 8
Route de la Falaise.

114
00:11:58.597 --> 00:12:00.160
Malcolm.

115
00:12:00.165 --> 00:12:02.165
Malcolm. Malcolm.

116
00:12:07.973 --> 00:12:10.407
I asked you for your
price. What is this?

117
00:12:10.609 --> 00:12:12.606
A man who might be interested...

118
00:12:12.611 --> 00:12:14.670
in taking the job.
This man will.

119
00:12:15.213 --> 00:12:17.213
My boss said you're
the man for the job.

120
00:12:17.249 --> 00:12:19.249
Your boss got his facts wrong.

121
00:12:21.319 --> 00:12:23.319
Two things you should
know about my boss:

122
00:12:23.522 --> 00:12:25.083
He never gets his facts wrong,

123
00:12:25.088 --> 00:12:26.953
he never takes no
for an answer.

124
00:12:26.958 --> 00:12:29.008
Well, there's a first
time for everything.

125
00:12:37.602 --> 00:12:40.696
Well, not this time.

126
00:12:46.945 --> 00:12:49.004
You don't wanna do this.

127
00:12:49.214 --> 00:12:51.256
I don't think you're
in a position to...

128
00:12:51.261 --> 00:12:53.261
tell me what I do
and don't wanna do.

129
00:12:53.351 --> 00:12:56.320
You have 10 seconds
to change your mind.

130
00:13:00.726 --> 00:13:04.093
I'll give you five seconds
to remove your hand.

131
00:14:03.989 --> 00:14:06.082
Malcolm. Malcolm.

132
00:14:06.291 --> 00:14:08.291
You hear me?

133
00:14:09.961 --> 00:14:12.361
Mal, I said drop in
anytime, but I didn't mean...

134
00:14:12.664 --> 00:14:15.360
- Nowhere else to go.
- Just take it easy, okay?

135
00:14:17.068 --> 00:14:18.498
Don't move me from the car.

136
00:14:18.503 --> 00:14:21.457
- It's just till the
ambulance arrives.

137
00:14:21.462 --> 00:14:23.336
No ambulance.

138
00:14:23.341 --> 00:14:24.912
You need a doctor, you've been...

139
00:14:24.917 --> 00:14:26.917
shot. I can't take
care of this.

140
00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.648
Not far from car.

141
00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:33.580
Relax.

142
00:14:33.585 --> 00:14:38.215
Just try to stay calm. We'll
have you fixed up in no time.

143
00:14:49.234 --> 00:14:51.259
He's inside.
Quick, it's serious.

144
00:14:55.841 --> 00:14:57.037
Sir?

145
00:14:57.042 --> 00:14:58.981
- You wanna be
careful moving him.

146
00:14:58.986 --> 00:15:00.440
We know our job, okay?

147
00:15:00.445 --> 00:15:02.936
Sir, can you hear me?

148
00:15:03.148 --> 00:15:04.878
This car... No...

149
00:15:04.883 --> 00:15:06.847
If you hear me, press my hand.

150
00:15:06.852 --> 00:15:08.852
The car...

151
00:15:58.336 --> 00:16:00.336
Am I in heaven?

152
00:16:01.039 --> 00:16:03.039
Actually, you're in
a bit of the shit.

153
00:16:03.642 --> 00:16:06.133
You'll help me out of it?

154
00:16:06.845 --> 00:16:08.845
That depends on
how deep you're in.

155
00:16:08.947 --> 00:16:10.258
- Don't trust anyone.

156
00:16:10.263 --> 00:16:12.263
Couldn't agree with you more.

157
00:16:14.319 --> 00:16:16.082
- Come on.
- No. Don't leave the car.

158
00:16:16.087 --> 00:16:18.245
- What's so special
about the car?

159
00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:20.250
Not the car.

160
00:16:31.436 --> 00:16:33.436
Wait.

161
00:17:02.033 --> 00:17:04.033
I told you.

162
00:17:08.173 --> 00:17:10.173
Don't trust anyone.

163
00:17:11.543 --> 00:17:13.543
I told you.

164
00:18:05.563 --> 00:18:07.690
I took the liberty
of bringing your suit.

165
00:18:07.899 --> 00:18:10.249
It's what you wear when
you're working, correct?

166
00:18:10.268 --> 00:18:12.930
Correct. But I'm not working.

167
00:18:13.471 --> 00:18:16.565
- You see, boss? I told you.
- Please, Joseph.

168
00:18:17.275 --> 00:18:19.325
Your approach was not
very effective in...

169
00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.330
presenting our proposal
the first time.

170
00:18:21.446 --> 00:18:23.446
Thank you.

171
00:18:23.681 --> 00:18:24.878
As I was saying...

172
00:18:24.883 --> 00:18:26.495
...we came to you
in good faith.

173
00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:28.214
You said you were unavailable.

174
00:18:28.219 --> 00:18:30.769
We contracted with the man
whose number you gave us.

175
00:18:30.855 --> 00:18:32.585
He proved to be ineffective.

176
00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:35.855
And now I am left with
unfinished business.

177
00:18:36.061 --> 00:18:38.359
The way I see it,
you're responsible.

178
00:18:38.863 --> 00:18:40.888
I understand your
point of view.

179
00:18:41.099 --> 00:18:43.099
But I'm still unavailable.

180
00:18:44.302 --> 00:18:46.302
Boss, can I say something?

181
00:18:48.606 --> 00:18:50.836
Anyone else wanna
say something?

182
00:18:53.978 --> 00:18:55.775
Good.

183
00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.805
Find me a smarter one.

184
00:19:00.151 --> 00:19:02.351
You have three seconds
to change your mind...

185
00:19:02.387 --> 00:19:05.151
...or you're gonna be
permanently unavailable.

186
00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.790
One.

187
00:19:09.627 --> 00:19:11.627
Two.

188
00:19:13.832 --> 00:19:15.832
One condition.

189
00:19:18.069 --> 00:19:20.069
I'm listening.

190
00:19:20.271 --> 00:19:22.466
I drive my own car.

191
00:19:23.775 --> 00:19:25.775
Deal.

192
00:19:28.546 --> 00:19:30.320
In anticipation of
your answer, we...

193
00:19:30.325 --> 00:19:32.145
took the liberty of
bringing your car.

194
00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.984
Changed the oil,
gave it a tune-up,

195
00:19:33.989 --> 00:19:36.086
took out all the
non-essential material.

196
00:19:36.287 --> 00:19:39.814
Left the switch-over
license plates. Love that.

197
00:19:40.024 --> 00:19:42.288
Replaced the GPS
with one of our own.

198
00:19:42.494 --> 00:19:44.494
Preprogrammed. More
efficient that way.

199
00:19:44.796 --> 00:19:46.956
Why I was so insistent
on using only...

200
00:19:46.961 --> 00:19:48.961
the best man for
this assignment?

201
00:19:51.536 --> 00:19:53.970
We're playing in a
much larger game here.

202
00:19:54.172 --> 00:19:56.776
Don't think of this
as just another...

203
00:19:56.781 --> 00:19:58.836
job. Think of it as a mission.

204
00:20:00.879 --> 00:20:02.487
I'm so pleased to
find we share...

205
00:20:02.492 --> 00:20:03.910
the same approach to our work.

206
00:20:03.915 --> 00:20:06.165
I make a deal, that's
the deal. Just like you.

207
00:20:06.183 --> 00:20:08.913
You don't like names. Neither
do I. We're both precise.

208
00:20:09.119 --> 00:20:10.905
Neither one of us
has any interest...

209
00:20:10.910 --> 00:20:12.417
in what we're paid to do...

210
00:20:12.422 --> 00:20:14.399
...beyond what we are paid to...

211
00:20:14.404 --> 00:20:16.404
do. Those are your
rules, right?

212
00:20:24.568 --> 00:20:26.568
You forgot one.

213
00:20:26.803 --> 00:20:27.803
- I work alone.

214
00:20:27.808 --> 00:20:29.808
I thought you might
like the company.

215
00:20:30.174 --> 00:20:32.472
Thought you wanted me
to complete a mission.

216
00:20:34.711 --> 00:20:36.711
You're right. I do.

217
00:20:39.283 --> 00:20:41.283
Wait.

218
00:20:42.386 --> 00:20:44.386
What, you wanna
change the rules?

219
00:20:45.923 --> 00:20:48.687
Every rule has an exception.
Let's make one for today.

220
00:20:51.929 --> 00:20:53.929
You're the boss.

221
00:20:55.866 --> 00:20:57.866
Anything else?

222
00:20:58.535 --> 00:21:00.535
The jewelry. Anything
I should know?

223
00:21:04.007 --> 00:21:06.757
You remember those jokers
trying to blow up airliners...

224
00:21:06.843 --> 00:21:09.693
...by sneaking liquids through
and combining them onboard?

225
00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:11.880
Same principle, just refined.

226
00:21:11.982 --> 00:21:13.879
Twenty-five feet
from the car...

227
00:21:13.884 --> 00:21:15.275
...yellow light comes on,

228
00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.285
signaling the first
liquid is ready.

229
00:21:17.487 --> 00:21:19.487
Fifty feet, orange.

230
00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.020
Second liquid flows
into the chamber.

231
00:21:22.025 --> 00:21:24.994
Seventy-five feet,
you're gonna see red.

232
00:21:30.234 --> 00:21:32.234
Time to go.

233
00:21:32.502 --> 00:21:36.199
This phone is programmed to
call only one number, mine.

234
00:21:37.274 --> 00:21:39.231
When you pass the
first toll on the...

235
00:21:39.236 --> 00:21:41.236
road going north,
call me, all right?

236
00:21:42.246 --> 00:21:45.215
Money for gas and food.

237
00:21:45.415 --> 00:21:47.415
Any other questions?

238
00:22:18.248 --> 00:22:20.409
Would you mind
buckling your seat belt?

239
00:22:31.328 --> 00:22:34.491
Don't suppose you wanna tell
me what this is all about?

240
00:22:40.304 --> 00:22:42.304
Great.

241
00:22:57.921 --> 00:23:00.481
Ocean Pearl requesting
cargo clearance.

242
00:23:02.192 --> 00:23:04.683
The papers are with the
environmental agency.

243
00:23:05.095 --> 00:23:07.095
Drop anchor and wait to dock.

244
00:23:07.197 --> 00:23:08.820
- We'll inform you
when they're signed.

245
00:23:08.825 --> 00:23:10.825
Okay.

246
00:23:19.409 --> 00:23:21.306
I know what happened to you.

247
00:23:21.311 --> 00:23:23.541
But what happened to Frank?

248
00:23:29.286 --> 00:23:31.416
Colonel Medved over
at Intelligence...

249
00:23:31.421 --> 00:23:33.421
has been given all
the information.

250
00:23:34.057 --> 00:23:35.587
He knows it's top priority.

251
00:23:35.592 --> 00:23:38.152
He wants you to know he
has his best men on it.

252
00:23:38.362 --> 00:23:40.523
He'll keep it out
of official channels.

253
00:23:40.731 --> 00:23:44.394
He suggests you buy as
much time as you can.

254
00:24:39.856 --> 00:24:42.231
Look, I don't know what
your part in all...

255
00:24:42.236 --> 00:24:44.555
this is or isn't. And
I don't really care.

256
00:24:44.761 --> 00:24:47.061
You were here first, you
know more than I do...

257
00:24:47.264 --> 00:24:49.161
...download me
on what you know.

258
00:24:49.166 --> 00:24:50.929
I know nothing.

259
00:24:50.934 --> 00:24:53.129
How did you know Malcolm?

260
00:24:53.570 --> 00:24:55.133
I didn't.

261
00:24:55.138 --> 00:24:56.709
You just happened to end up in...

262
00:24:56.714 --> 00:24:58.714
a car with a man
you don't know?

263
00:25:00.177 --> 00:25:02.270
I'm now in a car
with man I don't know.

264
00:25:04.147 --> 00:25:06.775
Aren't you supposed
to make a call?

265
00:25:13.156 --> 00:25:14.820
Nice to hear from you.

266
00:25:14.825 --> 00:25:17.885
You can skip the pleasantries.
Just give me the code.

267
00:25:18.228 --> 00:25:20.228
1- 1-
2-6.

268
00:25:24.100 --> 00:25:26.500
Call me when you arrive.

269
00:25:28.305 --> 00:25:30.671
What's in Budapest?

270
00:25:30.874 --> 00:25:33.138
Goulash. Beer.

271
00:25:40.150 --> 00:25:41.580
All right.

272
00:25:41.585 --> 00:25:44.383
Let's rewind here, start
with the proper introductions.

273
00:25:45.021 --> 00:25:47.546
What happened to
the rule of no names?

274
00:25:47.757 --> 00:25:50.817
I'm suspending that
rule for the moment.

275
00:25:53.897 --> 00:25:56.092
I'm Frank Martin.

276
00:25:58.401 --> 00:26:00.401
And your name is?

277
00:26:03.039 --> 00:26:05.405
What matters, my name?

278
00:26:06.009 --> 00:26:08.910
Well, we're in this
situation together.

279
00:26:09.479 --> 00:26:11.479
No.

280
00:26:13.683 --> 00:26:15.604
We're sitting here
with two exploding...

281
00:26:15.609 --> 00:26:17.609
bracelets on, going
to the same place.

282
00:26:18.588 --> 00:26:20.638
I'd call that being
in the same situation.

283
00:26:20.991 --> 00:26:23.551
It's not. They are
going to kill you.

284
00:26:25.562 --> 00:26:27.562
I'm aware of that.

285
00:26:28.532 --> 00:26:30.105
In all probability, after they...

286
00:26:30.110 --> 00:26:31.730
kill me, you're
next on the list.

287
00:26:31.735 --> 00:26:33.413
Now, if I'm gonna
keep that from...

288
00:26:33.418 --> 00:26:35.418
happening, I'm gonna
need a little help.

289
00:26:35.472 --> 00:26:38.100
From the top. We
have this problem.

290
00:26:38.308 --> 00:26:40.308
You think I don't
know it's a problem?

291
00:26:40.744 --> 00:26:42.744
I look stupid to you?

292
00:26:43.313 --> 00:26:45.804
I didn't say you were stupid.

293
00:26:47.551 --> 00:26:49.114
But we have a problem...

294
00:26:49.119 --> 00:26:50.992
...and you're not
being very helpful...

295
00:26:50.997 --> 00:26:52.997
in participating in
the solution of it.

296
00:26:54.457 --> 00:26:56.721
I don't want to talk anymore.

297
00:27:04.100 --> 00:27:06.100
Fine.

298
00:27:18.748 --> 00:27:20.748
What did you say
your name was?

299
00:27:21.451 --> 00:27:24.420
Frank. Frank Martin.

300
00:27:25.422 --> 00:27:27.549
Frank Martin.

301
00:27:27.924 --> 00:27:29.949
Valentina.

302
00:27:33.029 --> 00:27:35.520
Pleased to meet you.

303
00:28:31.521 --> 00:28:33.682
The gentlemen from
Ecocorp are here.

304
00:28:35.158 --> 00:28:37.158
Show them in.

305
00:28:44.134 --> 00:28:46.134
Gentlemen.

306
00:28:48.405 --> 00:28:50.135
Mr. Minister.

307
00:28:50.140 --> 00:28:53.007
We'd like to thank you for
reconsidering our proposal...

308
00:28:53.209 --> 00:28:54.536
...on such short notice.

309
00:28:54.541 --> 00:28:56.341
You make it very hard not to.

310
00:28:56.346 --> 00:28:58.318
Well, yes. We do
have a reputation...

311
00:28:58.323 --> 00:29:00.323
of not taking no
for an answer.

312
00:29:00.917 --> 00:29:02.917
Here are the contracts.

313
00:29:04.254 --> 00:29:06.151
All in order.

314
00:29:06.156 --> 00:29:08.356
We were told the ships
couldn't be cleared...

315
00:29:08.391 --> 00:29:10.541
...unless you personally
signed off on them.

316
00:29:10.593 --> 00:29:12.490
Ships?

317
00:29:12.495 --> 00:29:14.125
I thought there was only one.

318
00:29:14.130 --> 00:29:16.598
Oh, well, here's the thing.

319
00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:19.530
In order to make the
venture more profitable...

320
00:29:19.736 --> 00:29:21.499
...we need to process
the material...

321
00:29:21.504 --> 00:29:22.901
in a volume that makes sense.

322
00:29:22.906 --> 00:29:24.736
How many ships are
we talking about?

323
00:29:24.741 --> 00:29:28.507
Plus the one in the port
waiting on clearance, eight.

324
00:29:29.145 --> 00:29:30.709
Eight.

325
00:29:30.714 --> 00:29:32.714
This year.

326
00:29:33.149 --> 00:29:36.175
Protecting the environment
is a long-term commitment.

327
00:29:36.386 --> 00:29:38.386
You've said so
yourself, haven't you?

328
00:29:38.588 --> 00:29:41.113
And I will do again
tomorrow in Odessa...

329
00:29:41.324 --> 00:29:44.191
...where I will sign these.

330
00:29:45.161 --> 00:29:47.925
We were really hoping
to settle this today.

331
00:29:48.131 --> 00:29:52.500
I want to review them, now
that there are some addendums.

332
00:29:52.702 --> 00:29:54.952
Twenty-four hours doesn't
make a difference...

333
00:29:55.071 --> 00:29:57.437
...on such a long-term
commitment, will it?

334
00:29:58.208 --> 00:30:00.904
No, of course not.

335
00:30:01.111 --> 00:30:05.104
Then I will see you tomorrow
in Odessa. Let's say 9 a. m.

336
00:30:10.987 --> 00:30:12.584
Yes.

337
00:30:12.589 --> 00:30:14.519
Okay, I'll stay.

338
00:30:14.524 --> 00:30:16.354
- But the material is leaking.
- And?

339
00:30:16.359 --> 00:30:19.009
- We won't be able to hide it.
- I'll take care of it.

340
00:30:19.129 --> 00:30:20.625
If ever they check...

341
00:30:20.630 --> 00:30:22.928
Easy. The deal will
be closed very soon.

342
00:30:23.133 --> 00:30:25.133
Twenty-four hours. No more.

343
00:30:33.877 --> 00:30:34.877
- Yes?

344
00:30:34.882 --> 00:30:37.643
I've bought you
another 24 hours.

345
00:30:37.847 --> 00:30:40.145
You have until
tomorrow, 9 a. m.

346
00:30:40.350 --> 00:30:42.350
That should be more
than enough time.

347
00:30:42.786 --> 00:30:44.786
Do you have a lead?

348
00:30:44.821 --> 00:30:46.821
Better than a lead.

349
00:30:47.457 --> 00:30:49.457
A location.

350
00:31:27.030 --> 00:31:29.030
I'm hungry.

351
00:31:30.033 --> 00:31:32.524
We're 100 kilometers
from beer and sausage.

352
00:31:34.003 --> 00:31:36.403
I don't like sausage.

353
00:31:39.209 --> 00:31:41.209
What would you like?

354
00:31:45.315 --> 00:31:47.145
Veal.

355
00:31:47.150 --> 00:31:49.150
Roast, with carrots...

356
00:31:49.285 --> 00:31:51.285
...and beets.

357
00:31:52.288 --> 00:31:55.314
In gravy, with
Madeira in stock.

358
00:31:55.525 --> 00:31:57.525
Nothing to start?

359
00:32:00.363 --> 00:32:02.363
A salad.

360
00:32:02.965 --> 00:32:06.196
Greens tossed with balsamic.

361
00:32:06.401 --> 00:32:08.365
From Modena.

362
00:32:08.370 --> 00:32:09.967
Aged?

363
00:32:09.972 --> 00:32:11.972
Of course, aged.

364
00:32:14.977 --> 00:32:16.977
And for dessert?

365
00:32:18.247 --> 00:32:20.247
Sachertorte.

366
00:32:20.382 --> 00:32:22.873
With whipped cream or without?

367
00:32:24.253 --> 00:32:26.253
With.

368
00:32:26.388 --> 00:32:28.388
To drink?

369
00:32:30.158 --> 00:32:31.555
Wine.

370
00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:33.560
Tokaj, perhaps?

371
00:32:33.896 --> 00:32:35.896
Ice wine.

372
00:32:36.131 --> 00:32:38.131
Of course.

373
00:32:49.845 --> 00:32:50.951
- What are you doing?

374
00:32:50.956 --> 00:32:52.956
Seeing a man about
some jewelry.

375
00:33:04.359 --> 00:33:06.359
He's gone off the reservation.

376
00:33:08.263 --> 00:33:11.562
Send someone to
get him back on.

377
00:33:12.234 --> 00:33:14.234
Don't kill him.

378
00:33:40.896 --> 00:33:43.490
Frank. It's so good to
see you, 'mein Freund'.

379
00:33:43.799 --> 00:33:46.097
Good to see you too, Otto.

380
00:33:46.468 --> 00:33:48.959
You didn't mention
you bring company.

381
00:33:49.504 --> 00:33:51.168
It's not really company.

382
00:33:51.173 --> 00:33:53.173
It's...

383
00:33:54.009 --> 00:33:55.305
...complicated.

384
00:33:55.310 --> 00:33:57.008
With you, it's
always complicated.

385
00:33:57.013 --> 00:33:58.475
You can tell me about it...

386
00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:00.314
...over a nice schnitzel with...

387
00:34:00.319 --> 00:34:02.319
'Kartoffelsalat'
I have prepared.

388
00:34:02.851 --> 00:34:05.012
Hey, Otto, you know I
love your schnitzel...

389
00:34:05.220 --> 00:34:07.654
...but we need to
get rid of this first.

390
00:34:10.192 --> 00:34:11.504
Binary free-form...

391
00:34:11.509 --> 00:34:13.650
magnetic-resolution
technology.

392
00:34:14.162 --> 00:34:16.162
English, please, Otto.

393
00:34:16.832 --> 00:34:18.982
There's a program the
Pentagon has funded...

394
00:34:19.034 --> 00:34:22.128
...through one of their
subsidiary front companies...

395
00:34:22.337 --> 00:34:23.949
...that's been experimenting...

396
00:34:23.954 --> 00:34:25.869
with this new kind
of weaponry...

397
00:34:25.874 --> 00:34:28.502
...based on the theory
of magnetic attraction.

398
00:34:28.710 --> 00:34:30.735
Very hush-hush stuff.

399
00:34:32.414 --> 00:34:34.054
I didn't realize
you were in the...

400
00:34:34.059 --> 00:34:35.512
loop on the
Pentagon hush-hush.

401
00:34:35.517 --> 00:34:37.717
You wouldn't believe
what you can discover...

402
00:34:37.753 --> 00:34:39.914
...walking through
the Internet.

403
00:34:40.122 --> 00:34:42.352
You wanna see the
invasion plans for Iran?

404
00:34:42.824 --> 00:34:44.755
Maybe some other time.

405
00:34:44.760 --> 00:34:46.579
Right now we need to
get this thing...

406
00:34:46.584 --> 00:34:48.392
off without blowing
myself to Iran.

407
00:34:48.397 --> 00:34:50.831
I don't wanna bother
you with the details...

408
00:34:51.033 --> 00:34:55.561
...but usually there's a
transmitter plate close by.

409
00:35:01.777 --> 00:35:03.440
You should not be doing this.

410
00:35:03.445 --> 00:35:05.545
First you don't talk,
now you offer advice.

411
00:35:05.647 --> 00:35:08.115
Not advice. A warning.

412
00:35:08.450 --> 00:35:10.900
Well, a little late for
warnings, don't you think?

413
00:35:17.292 --> 00:35:19.292
I agree with you.

414
00:35:23.065 --> 00:35:25.065
You're off course.

415
00:35:30.739 --> 00:35:33.333
- Should I?
- Yeah, you should.

416
00:35:39.347 --> 00:35:41.347
Look, fellas...

417
00:35:41.750 --> 00:35:44.651
...some things in the car were
a bit off, needed checking.

418
00:35:46.088 --> 00:35:48.588
In my profession, a man
is only as good as the car.

419
00:35:48.590 --> 00:35:51.787
You take care of the car,
the car will take care of you.

420
00:35:53.962 --> 00:35:56.294
The boss says,
'Back on the road.'

421
00:35:56.798 --> 00:35:58.798
Frank?

422
00:35:58.934 --> 00:36:00.934
Keep at it.

423
00:36:02.704 --> 00:36:04.501
Back in the car, Frank.

424
00:36:04.506 --> 00:36:06.506
No.

425
00:37:17.112 --> 00:37:19.171
- Find it?
- Not yet.

426
00:38:35.924 --> 00:38:37.721
You're the smart one?

427
00:38:37.726 --> 00:38:40.320
No. I'm the big one.

428
00:39:32.514 --> 00:39:34.514
Not so big anymore, are you?

429
00:39:56.438 --> 00:39:58.438
Found it.

430
00:40:02.477 --> 00:40:04.968
- The transmitter.
- Can you remove it?

431
00:40:07.482 --> 00:40:09.012
It's wired.

432
00:40:09.017 --> 00:40:11.017
If I do:

433
00:41:08.777 --> 00:41:10.802
You fight good.

434
00:41:13.848 --> 00:41:15.941
But you tie bad.

435
00:41:21.589 --> 00:41:23.119
Where are you going?

436
00:41:23.124 --> 00:41:25.124
Tired.

437
00:41:26.094 --> 00:41:28.289
That's why I prefer
to deal with cars.

438
00:41:29.164 --> 00:41:31.164
That makes two of us.

439
00:41:31.366 --> 00:41:34.335
What do you want me to do when
they...? When they wake up?

440
00:41:34.536 --> 00:41:37.596
Probably best to take
the rest of the day off.

441
00:41:55.957 --> 00:41:57.287
I'm not amused.

442
00:41:57.292 --> 00:41:59.342
You'd be less amused
if you ended up dead.

443
00:41:59.360 --> 00:42:01.760
If you wanted me dead,
I'd be dead. You need me.

444
00:42:01.963 --> 00:42:03.387
You want me to complete the...

445
00:42:03.392 --> 00:42:05.392
job, I need some
clarification.

446
00:42:06.401 --> 00:42:07.964
I'm listening.

447
00:42:07.969 --> 00:42:09.299
In person.

448
00:42:09.304 --> 00:42:10.934
We've already done in person.

449
00:42:10.939 --> 00:42:13.032
Well, not to my
satisfaction, apparently.

450
00:42:13.775 --> 00:42:16.676
Right now, my satisfaction
should be your main concern.

451
00:42:17.779 --> 00:42:20.304
Same place. One hour.
Wait for my call.

452
00:43:17.205 --> 00:43:18.468
Hello?

453
00:43:18.473 --> 00:43:20.473
You've disappointed me.

454
00:43:20.608 --> 00:43:23.668
You won't be the first
and you won't be the last.

455
00:43:23.878 --> 00:43:26.503
- I told you I wanted
to do this in person.

456
00:43:26.508 --> 00:43:28.645
That won't be
necessary. You see...

457
00:43:28.850 --> 00:43:31.000
...since our little
chat at the beginning...

458
00:43:31.119 --> 00:43:32.892
...I've been thinking
I don't need...

459
00:43:32.897 --> 00:43:34.817
the best for this
mundane assignment.

460
00:43:34.822 --> 00:43:36.983
Any idiot with a
driver's license will do.

461
00:43:37.191 --> 00:43:40.217
So in the words of the
great American, Donald Trump:

462
00:43:40.428 --> 00:43:43.761
I'm sorry, but you're fired.

463
00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:31.540
Who are you?

464
00:44:31.545 --> 00:44:34.139
- Your new chauffeur.
- I want the old one back.

465
00:44:34.348 --> 00:44:36.680
He's about to go to pieces.

466
00:45:45.152 --> 00:45:47.152
You're fired.

467
00:45:50.323 --> 00:45:51.720
How was your nap?

468
00:45:51.725 --> 00:45:54.125
Restful. How was
your phone call?

469
00:45:54.327 --> 00:45:56.795
Brief. Fasten your seat belt.

470
00:46:08.709 --> 00:46:09.905
Tarconi.

471
00:46:09.910 --> 00:46:11.910
It's me.

472
00:46:12.112 --> 00:46:14.042
I was wondering
when you would call.

473
00:46:14.047 --> 00:46:15.444
I've been busy.

474
00:46:15.449 --> 00:46:18.077
Let me guess. In Budapest?

475
00:46:19.352 --> 00:46:21.183
You've been busy too.

476
00:46:21.188 --> 00:46:24.021
Never a problem keeping that
way with a friend like you.

477
00:46:24.224 --> 00:46:25.414
So I don't have to be...

478
00:46:25.419 --> 00:46:27.255
redundant, tell
me what you know.

479
00:46:27.260 --> 00:46:29.694
There is a black
Mercedes also in Budapest.

480
00:46:29.896 --> 00:46:31.955
Probably not occupied
by friends of yours.

481
00:46:32.165 --> 00:46:34.793
That is what I know. Now
tell me what you know.

482
00:46:35.602 --> 00:46:38.935
I have two bags in the back
and a girl in the front.

483
00:46:39.139 --> 00:46:41.139
Russian, I think.

484
00:46:41.274 --> 00:46:43.524
I don't know what she
has to do with anything.

485
00:46:43.643 --> 00:46:45.643
Have you tried asking her?

486
00:46:45.812 --> 00:46:47.871
Now, why didn't
I think of that?

487
00:46:47.881 --> 00:46:50.031
Sorry. Of course you've
asked. And she says?

488
00:46:50.417 --> 00:46:51.913
I'm going to die.

489
00:46:51.918 --> 00:46:54.216
Typical. Russians.

490
00:46:54.421 --> 00:46:56.616
They are so dark.

491
00:46:56.823 --> 00:47:00.315
I remember, in school, reading
Dostoyevsky and thinking...

492
00:47:00.527 --> 00:47:03.189
...when do these people laugh?

493
00:47:03.396 --> 00:47:05.260
One page after the other...

494
00:47:05.265 --> 00:47:08.234
...misery and suffering like
you wouldn't believe, Frank.

495
00:47:08.435 --> 00:47:09.927
Inspector, can we save the...

496
00:47:09.932 --> 00:47:11.932
literature lesson?
I'm blinking here.

497
00:47:12.038 --> 00:47:14.038
Is that code?

498
00:47:14.174 --> 00:47:17.610
No, it's some bracelet
they accessorized us with.

499
00:47:17.811 --> 00:47:20.161
Wired to explode if we
get too far from the car.

500
00:47:20.247 --> 00:47:21.943
They?

501
00:47:21.948 --> 00:47:23.211
Some American.

502
00:47:23.216 --> 00:47:26.049
Can you be more specific?
A name? A number?

503
00:47:26.253 --> 00:47:27.482
Nothing.

504
00:47:27.487 --> 00:47:29.682
Why do you always
make it so easy, Frank?

505
00:47:29.890 --> 00:47:31.787
It's my nature.

506
00:47:31.792 --> 00:47:33.792
Where are you? I
will come there.

507
00:47:33.827 --> 00:47:36.477
That's not a good idea. They
have me on a short leash.

508
00:47:36.496 --> 00:47:39.329
I can't be of much help if
you do not give me something.

509
00:47:40.967 --> 00:47:43.094
How close are
you to a computer?

510
00:47:46.940 --> 00:47:48.236
Yes, Frank?

511
00:47:48.241 --> 00:47:51.005
That wasn't very nice,
back there in the market.

512
00:47:51.211 --> 00:47:54.044
You were the one who
broke the rules, not me.

513
00:47:54.247 --> 00:47:56.306
Point well taken.

514
00:47:56.583 --> 00:48:00.110
That makes us even. What say
we start with a clean slate?

515
00:48:00.320 --> 00:48:03.448
So this call is about
kiss-and-make-up, then?

516
00:48:04.090 --> 00:48:05.353
More or less.

517
00:48:05.358 --> 00:48:08.259
You have what I need to
get the bracelet off...

518
00:48:08.461 --> 00:48:11.294
...I have the packages
you need delivered.

519
00:48:12.332 --> 00:48:14.857
Here are the new
coordinates, then: 2-6-12.

520
00:48:15.268 --> 00:48:16.932
That'll take you
to the place...

521
00:48:16.937 --> 00:48:19.437
...where we can have a
conclusion to this business.

522
00:48:19.439 --> 00:48:21.439
I look forward to it.

523
00:48:27.180 --> 00:48:28.677
Frank.

524
00:48:28.682 --> 00:48:30.682
